    "result_text": "The build passes. The audit log confirms the new identity: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping the per-city sequence numbers entirely, and moved every value derived from it onto the new identity.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (which produced `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence) with `customerCode(owner)`, which builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n  - `regionCode(owner)` derives REGION from the postcode (NSW/VIC/QLD ranges), falling back to the city-to-region table, then `UNKNOWN` \u2014 so REGION is never empty.\n  - `identityHash8(telephone, lastName)` returns the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (telephone is already normalized to E.164 at the call site).\n- The membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), its Luhn check digit (computed over digits in `customerCode`), and the audit log line (`customerCode={}`) all consume `customerCode` directly, so they now reflect the region-and-hash identity automatically.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- `locality(owner)` now returns the REGION component parsed from `customerCode`, so locality moves in lockstep with the identity. It retains a direct postcode/city fallback for records without an assigned code (e.g. seed data), preserving their existing `UNKNOWN` value.\n\nThe existing/new acceptance test (`customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
